{
  "tema": 6992,
  "slug": "habria-hecho",
  "titulo": "Habría + participle = would have done",
  "subtitulo": "Yo habría invitado a menos gente.",
  "foto": "t06.jpg",
  "regla": "Would have done = haber in the conditional (habría, habrías, habría, habríamos, habrían) + participle. Nothing goes between habría and the participle. In many sentences hubiera can replace habría, but not the other way around.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "habría / habrías / habría / habríamos / habrían",
            "+ participle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "English needs _would have_; Spanish just puts **haber** in the **conditional**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Nothing** goes between **habría** and the participle: no pronouns, no **no**, no subject."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In everyday Mexican Spanish you'll very often hear **hubiera** instead of **habría**: **yo hubiera invitado a menos gente**. Both are accepted in that slot."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "But **habría** can't replace **hubiera** where the subjunctive is required: **me alegró que te hubieran elegido**, never ~~que te habrían elegido~~."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **habría** + participle is a road not taken."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Yo ==habría invitado== a menos gente a la fiesta.",
              "en": "I would have invited fewer people to the party."
            },
            {
              "es": "Él no te ==habría querido== tanto como yo.",
              "en": "He wouldn't have loved you as much as I do."
            },
            {
              "es": "Dicen que ==habrían invertido== su dinero en otra cosa.",
              "en": "They say they would have invested their money in something else."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Qué ==habrías hecho== tú en mi lugar?",
              "en": "What would you have done in my place?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Ustedes ==habrían sido== más felices en Querétaro.",
              "en": "You would have been happier in Querétaro."
            },
            {
              "es": "A Antonio le ==habría gustado== estudiar medicina.",
              "en": "Antonio would have liked to study medicine."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hubiera",
      "titulo": "Habría or hubiera?",
      "bloques": [
